# {{name}}/.env.example --- copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# These load into the process environment via cons/env:load-project-env, which the
# generated entry point calls as its FIRST act -- before anything can read the
# environment. Keep it that way: a .env loaded lazily, wherever the first consumer
# happens to sit, is a .env that was not loaded for whatever ran before it, and that
# failure blames the library rather than the ordering.
#
# The host environment wins in prod (set real vars there, ship no .env). Add KEY=VALUE
# lines as the project needs them.

# EXAMPLE_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME
